Z||000004||80's BOY||07-10-2000||04:42 PM||||hey pollock, how's things in Denton?? did you cut out the space frame yet, or just the fiberglass? good luck my man. my Targa is AWESOME!! no matter how much you cuss your roof during the cut, it's worth it. BTW how did you choose to support your frame? if you need help i'm full of info.||||reg||10
Z||000005||dman||07-10-2000||06:29 PM||||Hi Pollock. Your t-top install sounds pretty cool! Do you need to strengthen the frame like you would if this was a convertible? Or does the T-Top install require just the roof cutting.<P>Hey 80's boy. I'm very interested in hearing more about your Targa project. I've been following its progress ever since you started posting about it a few months back (around May I think). I'm very interested in discussing frame strengthening with you, pollock, coyote, spyder and anyone else who is working on or considering a topless fiero. I just never seem to have the time to start a new topic.<P>I'm thinking about using 2x2 square tubing like coyote mentioned in a previous post of his. However I still have lots of little questions.<P>Hey pollock I hope you don't mind that I am using your post to start talking about frame strengthening. And by the way, continued good luck on your T-Top install. I can't wait to hear more about it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||TOM||07-10-2000||09:23 PM||||for a t-top install you get a steel center reinforce piece. So no frame work is needed. Only for targa or vert's do you need the stiffeners.||||reg||1
Z||000007||TOM||07-10-2000||09:25 PM||||one more thing. I hope its not too late. You need to install the center reinforce BEFORE you cut the steel space frame from above the windows.||||reg||1
Z||000008||007DOUG||07-11-2000||09:50 AM||||Here's a really crude (general) picture series of a T-Top install.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/ttopinstall.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/ttopinstall.html</A> <P><BR>I had the Fiero Factory install mine. They had the right tools (ie: frame flexers). If you don't have the flexers, place concrete blocks under the middle edges of the car to "flex" it during the "H" frame install.<P>No additional frame strengthening is needed. Once the "h" frame is installed, the constant (slight) flexing of the fiero spaceframe is all the support you need.<P>I've got another T-top here that I'm going to attempt install myself. I had the entire roof cutoff the donor fiero, and will use the attached roof & pillar parts as a template when cutting.<P>  First I'm going to try it on a junked space frame. I want to get some practice in first because if I cut too much off........yikes. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||pollock||07-11-2000||11:19 AM||||At this time, i'm not using any additional frame supports, but i plan to fab some subframe connectors out of steel tubing.<P>TOM, i wanted to do what you're suggesting:  install the H-frame before cutting the sides, but to my shagrin, it CANNOT be done that way.  You don't simply cut out the side pillars and utilize the sunroof opening.  You have to cut ALL the way across the back<BR>behind the opening and ALL the way across the front in front of the opening.  The H-frame won't go in before you do that.  It sucks.<P>So, i just placed a pair of jacks at the factory jack points on the rocker flanges.  I've only got the driver's side cut all the way, but i couldn't detect any movement or sag when i got all the way through.||||reg||1
Z||000010||pollock||07-11-2000||11:28 AM||||I just checked out doug's link....<P>Those "frame flexers" look like a fair way to keep the windshield frame from sagging, but i don't know how you could maneuver around them and continue to work on the car.  Plus, there's no way those could support the lower part of the chassis.  If you wanted a pair of those, you could whoop em up out of some cheapo turnbuckles.<P>BTW, the "crudity" of those photos reminded me of the ol' Haynes manual:  <BR>INSTRUCTIONS FOR TRANSAXLE REMOVAL:<BR>1. Remove wheels.<BR>2. Remove transaxle.<BR>3. Installation is reverse of removal.<P>LOL.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000011||007DOUG||07-11-2000||12:27 PM||||pollock<P>gotta love those manuals.....remove......install......what???<P>The frame flexers/supports used are actual C&C tools. The Fiero Factory has all the toys||||reg||1
